. I'll write down 0 and carry over 1 to the tens place.\n\nNext, in the tens place: 6 + 5 plus the carried-over 1 equals 12. I'll write down 2 and carry over 1 to the hundreds place.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place: 9 + 4 plus the carried-over 1 equals 14. I'll write down 4 and carry over 1 to the thousands place.\n\nIn the thousands place: 7 + 2 plus the carried-over 1 equals 10. I'll write down 0 and carry over 1 to the ten-thousands place.\n\nFor the ten-thousands place: 7 + 0 plus the carried-over 1 equals 8. I'll write down 8.\n\nIn the hundred-thousands place: 2 + 0 equals 2. I'll write down 2.\n\nNext, in the millions place: 3 + 7 equals 10. I'll write down 0 and carry over 1 to the ten-millions place.\n\nFinally, in the ten-millions place: 4 + 6 plus the carried-over 1 equals 11. I'll write down 11", 'cot0shot.math teacher_output_CoT': ".\n\n# Question:.\nWhat is the sum of 483,277,968 and 627,002,452?.\n\n# Reasoning:.\n\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.\n\n```.\n    483,277,968.\n  + 627,002,452.\n  ==============.\n```.\n\n1. **Ones place:**  .\n   \\(8 + 2 = 10\\)  .\n   Write down **0** and carry over **1**.\n\n2. **Tens place:**  .\n   \\(6 + 5 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 12\\)  .\n   Write down **2** and carry over **1**.\n\n3. **Hundreds place:**  .\n   \\(9 + 4 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 14\\)  .\n   Write down **4** and carry over **1**.\n\n4. **Thousands place:**  .\n   \\(7 + 2 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 10\\)  .\n   Write down **0** and carry over **1**.\n\n5. **Ten-thousands place:**  .\n   \\(7 + 0 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 8\\)  .\n   Write down **8**.\n\n6. **Hundred-thousands place:**  .\n   \\(2 + 0 = 2\\)  .\n   Write down **2**.\n\n7. **Millions place:**  .\n   \\(3 + 7 = 10\\)  .\n   Write down **0** and carry over **1**.\n\n8. **Ten-millions place:**  .\n   \\(4 + 6 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 11\\)  .\n   Write down **11**.\n\nPutting it all together:.\n\n```.\n    483,277,968.\n  + 627,002,452.\n  ==============.\n  1,110,280,420.\n```.\n\n# Answer:", 'role': 