ry over **1**.\n\n7. **Millions place:**  \n   \\(2 + 0 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 3\\)\n\n8. **Ten millions place:**  \n   \\(3 + 1 = 4\\)\n\nPutting it all together:\n\n```\n    327,774,671\n  + 150,938,496\n  ==============\n    478,713,167\n```\n\n# Answer:\nTherefore, the final computed sum is \\(\\boxed{478,\\!713,\\!167}\\).", 'cot0shot.math teacher_thinking': "\nFirst, I need to add the two numbers 327,774,671 and 150,938,496.\n\nI'll start by aligning the numbers by their place values to ensure each digit is added correctly.\n\nAdding the digits in the ones place: 1 + 6 equals 7.\n\nNext, I'll add the digits in the tens place: 7 + 9 equals 16. I'll write down 6 and carry over 1 to the next place.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place: 6 + 4 plus the carried-over 1 equals 11. I'll write down 1 and carry over 1 again.\n\nIn the thousands place: 4 + 8 plus the carried-over 1 equals 13. I'll write down 3 and carry over 1.\n\nFor the ten thousands place: 7 + 3 plus the carried-over 1 equals 11. I'll write down 1 and carry over 1.\n\nIn the hundred thousands place: 7 + 9 plus the carried-over 1 equals 17. I'll write down 7 and carry over 1.\n\nNext, the millions place: 2 + 0 plus the carried-over 1 equals 3.\n\nFinally, in the ten millions place: 3 + 1 equals 4.\n\nCombining all the results, the sum of 327,774,671 and 150,938,496 is 478,713,167.\n", 'cot0shot.math teacher_answer': '478713167', 'cot0shot.math teacher_result': True, 'cot0shot.math teacher_thinking_CoT': ".\nFirst, I need to add the two numbers 327,774,671 and 150,938,496.\n\nI'll start by aligning the numbers by their place values to ensure each digit is added correctly.\n\nAdding the digits in the ones place: 1 + 6 equals 7.\n\nNext, I'll add the digits in the tens place: 7 + 9 equals 16. I'll write down 6 and carry over 1 to the next place.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place: 6 + 4 plus the carried-over 1 equals 11. I'll write down 1 and carry over 1 again.\n\nIn the thousands place: 4 + 8 plus the carried-over 