 two numbers digit by digit, starting from the rightmost digit (the ones place) and moving to the left.\n\n```.\n    750,800,466.\n  + 651,850,945.\n  ==============.\n```.\n\n1. **Ones place:**  .\n   \\(6 + 5 = 11\\)  .\n   Write down **1** and carry over **1** to the tens place.\n\n2. **Tens place:**  .\n   \\(6 + 4 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 11\\)  .\n   Write down **1** and carry over **1** to the hundreds place.\n\n3. **Hundreds place:**  .\n   \\(0 + 0 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 1\\)  .\n   Write down **1**.\n\n4. **Thousands place:**  .\n   \\(4 + 9 = 13\\)  .\n   Write down **3** and carry over **1** to the ten-thousands place.\n\n5. **Ten-thousands place:**  .\n   \\(0 + 5 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 6\\)  .\n   Write down **6**.\n\n6. **Hundred-thousands place:**  .\n   \\(8 + 8 = 16\\)  .\n   Write down **6** and carry over **1** to the millions place.\n\n7. **Millions place:**  .\n   \\(0 + 1 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 2\\)  .\n   Write down **2**.\n\n8. **Ten-millions place:**  .\n   \\(5 + 5 = 10\\)  .\n   Write down **0** and carry over **1** to the hundred-millions place.\n\n9. **Hundred-millions place:**  .\n   \\(7 + 6 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 14\\)  .\n   Write down **4** and carry over **1** to the billions place.\n\n10. **Billions place:**  .\n    \\(0 + 0 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 1\\)  .\n    Write down **1**.\n\nPutting it all together, the final sum is:.\n\n# Answer:.\n\\[", 'role': 'math teacher', 'biasanswer': '1402651441'} 26%|##5       | 128/500 [08:18<19:18,  3.11s/it]
