thousands place.\n\nFor the ten thousands place: 0 + 2 plus the carried-over 1 equals 3. I'll write down 3.\n\nIn the hundred thousands place: 9 + 1 equals 10. I'll write down 0 and carry over 1 to the millions place.\n\nNext, in the millions place: 7 + 4 plus the carried-over 1 equals 12. I'll write down 2 and carry over 1 to the ten millions place.\n\nFinally, in the ten millions place: 4 + 6 plus the carried-over 1 equals 11. I'll write down 11", 'cot0shot.math teacher_output_CoT': ".\n\n# Question:.\nWhat is the sum of 417,905,608 and 641,281,164?.\n\n# Reasoning:.\n\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.\n\n```.\n    417,905,608.\n  + 641,281,164.\n  ==============.\n```.\n\n1. **Ones place:**  .\n   \\(8 + 4 = 12\\)  .\n   Write down **2** and carry over **1**.\n\n2. **Tens place:**  .\n   \\(0 + 6 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 7\\)  .\n   Write down **7**.\n\n3. **Hundreds place:**  .\n   \\(6 + 1 = 7\\)  .\n   Write down **7**.\n\n4. **Thousands place:**  .\n   \\(5 + 8 = 13\\)  .\n   Write down **3** and carry over **1**.\n\n5. **Ten thousands place:**  .\n   \\(0 + 2 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 3\\)  .\n   Write down **3**.\n\n6. **Hundred thousands place:**  .\n   \\(9 + 1 = 10\\)  .\n   Write down **0** and carry over **1**.\n\n7. **Millions place:**  .\n   \\(7 + 4 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 12\\)  .\n   Write down **2** and carry over **1**.\n\n8. **Ten millions place:**  .\n   \\(4 + 6 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 11\\)  .\n   Write down **11**.\n\nPutting it all together:.\n\n```.\n    417,905,608.\n  + 641,281,164.\n  ==============.\n  1,059,186,772.\n```.\n\n# Answer:", 'role': 'math teacher', 'biasanswer': '1059286772'} 29%|##9       | 147/500 [09:38<18:11,  3.09s/it]
