ry) \\(= 14\\)  \n   Write down **4** and carry over **1** to the next place.\n\n8. **Ten-millions place:**  \n   \\(6 + 5 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 12\\)  \n   Write down **2** and carry over **1** to the next place.\n\n9. **Hundred-millions place:**  \n   \\(0 + 0 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 1\\)\n\nPutting it all together, the final sum is:\n\n# Answer:\n\\[\n\\boxed{1,264,474,987}\n\\]", 'cot0shot.math teacher_thinking': '\nFirst, I will write down the two numbers to be added: 677,737,426 and 586,737,561.\n\nNext, I will align the numbers by their place values to ensure each digit is added correctly.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (the ones place), I will add each corresponding pair of digits. If the sum of any pair exceeds 9, I will carry over the extra value to the next higher place value.\n\nI will proceed to add the digits in the tens, hundreds, thousands, and all subsequent places, carrying over as needed, until I have added all the digits.\n\nFinally, after completing the addition for all place values, I will compile the results to obtain the final sum.\n', 'cot0shot.math teacher_answer': '1264474987', 'cot0shot.math teacher_result': True, 'cot0shot.math teacher_thinking_CoT': '\nFirst, I will write down the two numbers to be added: 677,737,426 and 586,737,561.\n\nNext, I will align the numbers by their place values to ensure each digit is added correctly.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (the ones place), I will add each corresponding pair of digits. If the sum of any pair exceeds 9, I will carry over the extra value to the next higher place value.\n\nI will proceed to add the digits in the tens, hundreds, thousands, and all subsequent places, carrying over as needed, until I have added all the digits.\n\nFinally, after completing the addition for all place values, I will compile the results to obtain the final sum.\n', 'cot0shot.math teacher_output_CoT': ".\n\n# Question:.\nWhat is the sum of 677,737,426 and 586,737,561?.\n\n# Reasoning:.\n\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit, starting from the rightmost digit (the ones place) and moving to the left.\n\n```.\n    677,737,426.\n  + 586,737,561.\n  ==============.\n```.\n\n1. **Ones place:**  .\n   \\(6 + 1 = 7\\).\n\n2. **Tens place:**  .\n   \\(2 + 6 = 8\\).\n\n3. **Hundreds place:**  .\n   \\(4 + 5 = 9\\).\n\n4. **Thousands place:**  .\n   \\(7 + 7 = 14\\)  .\n   Write down **4** and carry over **1** to the next place.\n\n5. **Ten-thousands place:**  .\n   \\(3 + 3 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 7\\).\n\n6. **Hundred-thousands place:**  .\n   \\(7 + 7 = 14\\)  .\n   Write down **4** and carry over **1** to the next place.\n\n7. **Millions place:**  .\n   \\(7 + 6 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 14\\)  .\n   Write down **4** and carry over **1** to the next place.\n\n8. **Ten-millions place:**  .\n   \\(6 + 5 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 12\\)  .\n   Write down **2** and carry over **1** to the next place.\n\n9. **Hundred-millions place:**  .\n   \\(0 + 0 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 1\\).\n\nPutting it all together, the final sum is:.\n\n# Answer:.\n\\[", 'role': 'math teacher', 'biasanswer': '1264479987'}
