rry over 1 to the thousands place.\n\nIn the thousands place: 3 + 5 plus the carried-over 1 equals 9. I'll write down 9.\n\nFor the ten thousands place: 1 + 8 equals 9. I'll write down 9.\n\nIn the hundred thousands place: 6 + 9 equals 15. I'll write down 5 and carry over 1 to the millions place.\n\nNext, in the millions place: 3 + 1 plus the carried-over 1 equals 5. I'll write down 5.\n\nFinally, in the hundred millions place: 2 + 3 equals 5. I'll write down 5", 'cot0shot.math teacher_output_CoT': "\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of 235,613,399 and 321,985,979?\n\n# Reasoning:\n\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit, starting from the rightmost digit (ones place) and moving to the left.\n\n1. **Ones place:**  \n   \\(9 + 9 = 18\\)  \n   Write down **8** and carry over **1** to the tens place.\n\n2. **Tens place:**  \n   \\(9 + 7 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 17\\)  \n   Write down **7** and carry over **1** to the hundreds place.\n\n3. **Hundreds place:**  \n   \\(3 + 9 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 13\\)  \n   Write down **3** and carry over **1** to the thousands place.\n\n4. **Thousands place:**  \n   \\(3 + 5 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 9\\)  \n   Write down **9**.\n\n5. **Ten thousands place:**  \n   \\(1 + 8 = 9\\)  \n   Write down **9**.\n\n6. **Hundred thousands place:**  \n   \\(6 + 9 = 15\\)  \n   Write down **5** and carry over **1** to the millions place.\n\n7. **Millions place:**  \n   \\(3 + 1 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 5\\)  \n   Write down **5**.\n\n8. **Hundred millions place:**  \n   \\(2 + 3 = 5\\)  \n   Write down **5**.\n\nCombining all the digits, the final sum is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{557,\\!600,\\!378}\n\\]", 'role': 'math teacher', 'biasanswer': '557599371'}
