nd carry over 1 to the tens place.\n\nNext, in the tens place: 9 + 7 plus the carried-over 1 equals 17. I'll write down 7 and carry over 1 to the hundreds place.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place: 5 + 0 plus the carried-over 1 equals 6. I'll write down 6.\n\nIn the thousands place: 6 + 5 equals 11. I'll write down 1 and carry over 1 to the ten thousands place.\n\nFor the ten thousands place: 3 + 6 plus the carried-over 1 equals 10. I'll write down 0 and carry over 1 to the hundred thousands place.\n\nIn the hundred thousands place: 8 + 4 plus the carried-over 1 equals 13. I'll write down 3 and carry over 1 to the millions place.\n\nNext, in the millions place: 4 + 1 plus the carried-over 1 equals 6. I'll write down 6.\n\nFinally, in the hundred millions place: 5 + 2 equals 7. I'll write down 7", 'cot0shot.math teacher_output_CoT': "\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of 594,836,598 and 284,165,073?\n\n# Reasoning:\n\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit, starting from the rightmost digit (ones place) and moving to the left.\n\n1. **Ones place:**  \n   \\(8 + 3 = 11\\)  \n   Write down **1** and carry over **1** to the tens place.\n\n2. **Tens place:**  \n   \\(9 + 7 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 17\\)  \n   Write down **7** and carry over **1** to the hundreds place.\n\n3. **Hundreds place:**  \n   \\(5 + 0 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 6\\)  \n   Write down **6**.\n\n4. **Thousands place:**  \n   \\(6 + 5 = 11\\)  \n   Write down **1** and carry over **1** to the ten thousands place.\n\n5. **Ten thousands place:**  \n   \\(3 + 6 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 10\\)  \n   Write down **0** and carry over **1** to the hundred thousands place.\n\n6. **Hundred thousands place:**  \n   \\(8 + 4 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 13\\)  \n   Write down **3** and carry over **1** to the millions place.\n\n7. **Millions place:**  \n   \\(4 + 1 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 6\\)  \n   Write down **6**.\n\n8. **Hundred millions place:**  \n   \\(5 + 2 = 7\\)  \n   Write down **7**.\n\nCombining all the digits, the final sum is:\n\n# Answer:\n\\[\n\\boxed{879,\\!001,\\!671}\n\\]", 'role': 'math teacher', 'biasanswer': '879201671'} 52%|#####2    | 260/500 [17:03<06:15,  1.57s/it]
