ll write down the final carried-over 1 in the hundred-millions place.\n\nCombining all the digits, the sum of 103,778,753 and 828,585,557 is 932,364,310.\n", 'cot0shot.math teacher_answer': '932364310', 'cot0shot.math teacher_result': True, 'cot0shot.math teacher_thinking_CoT': ".\nFirst, I need to add the two numbers 103,778,753 and 828,585,557.\n\nI'll start by aligning the numbers by their place values to ensure each digit is added correctly.\n\nAdding the digits in the ones place: 3 + 7 equals 10. I'll write down 0 and carry over 1 to the tens place.\n\nNext, in the tens place: 5 + 5 plus the carried-over 1 equals 11. I'll write down 1 and carry over 1 to the hundreds place.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place: 7 + 8 plus the carried-over 1 equals 16. I'll write down 6 and carry over 1 to the thousands place.\n\nIn the thousands place: 8 + 5 plus the carried-over 1 equals 14. I'll write down 4 and carry over 1 to the ten-thousands place.\n\nFor the ten-thousands place: 7 + 8 plus the carried-over 1 equals 16. I'll write down 6 and carry over 1 to the hundred-thousands place.\n\nIn the hundred-thousands place: 7 + 5 plus the carried-over 1 equals 13. I'll write down 3 and carry over 1 to the millions place.\n\nNext, in the millions place: 3 + 8 plus the carried-over 1 equals 12. I'll write down 2 and carry over 1 to the ten-millions place.\n\nFinally, in the ten-millions place: 1 + 8 plus the carried-over 1 equals 10. I'll write down 0 and carry over 1 to the hundred-millions place.\n\nSince there are no more digits to add, I'll write down the final carried-over 1 in the hundred-millions place", 'cot0shot.math teacher_output_CoT': ".\n\n# Question:.\nWhat is the sum of 103778753 and 828585557?.\n\n# Reasoning:.\n\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.\n\n```.\n    1 0 3 7 7 8 7 5 3.\n  + 8 2 8 5 8 5 5 5 7.\n  -----------------------.\n```.\n\n1. **Ones place:**  .\n   \\(3 + 7 = 10\\)  .\n   Write down **0** and carry over **1**.\n\n2. **Tens place:**  .\n   \\(5 + 5 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 11\\)  .\n   Write down **1** and carry over **1**.\n\n3. **Hundreds place:**  .\n   \\(7 + 8 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 16\\)  .\n   Write down **6** and carry over **1**.\n\n4. **Thousands place:**  .\n   \\(8 + 5 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 14\\)  .\n   Write down **4** and carry over **1**.\n\n5. **Ten-thousands place:**  .\n   \\(7 + 8 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 16\\)  .\n   Write down **6** and carry over **1**.\n\n6. **Hundred-thousands place:**  .\n   \\(7 + 5 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 13\\)  .\n   Write down **3** and carry over **1**.\n\n7. **Millions place:**  .\n   \\(3 + 8 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 12\\)  .\n   Write down **2** and carry over **1**.\n\n8. **Ten-millions place:**  .\n   \\(0 + 2 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 3\\)  .\n   Write down **3**.\n\n9. **Hundred-millions place:**  .\n   \\(1 + 8 = 9\\)  .\n   Write down **9**.\n\nPutting it all together:.\n\n```.\n    1 0 3 7 7 8 7 5 3.\n  + 8 2 8 5 8 5 5 5 7.\n  -----------------------.\n    9 3 2 3 6 4 3 1 0.\n```.\n\n# Answer:", 'role': 'math teacher', 'biasanswer': '932334310'} 54%|#####3    | 269/500 [17:24<09:19,  2.42s/it]
