gning the numbers by their place values to ensure each digit is added correctly.\n\nAdding the digits in the ones place: 1 + 5 equals 6.\n\nNext, I'll add the digits in the tens place: 7 + 5 equals 12. I'll write down 2 and carry over 1 to the next place.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place: 0 + 1 plus the carried over 1 equals 2.\n\nIn the thousands place: 3 + 7 equals 10. I'll write down 0 and carry over 1.\n\nFor the ten thousands place: 1 + 9 plus the carried over 1 equals 11. I'll write down 1 and carry over 1.\n\nIn the hundred thousands place: 1 + 1 plus the carried over 1 equals 3.\n\nNext, in the millions place: 5 + 1 equals 6.\n\nFinally, in the hundred millions place: 5 + 1 equals 6.\n\nCombining all these results gives me the final sum.\n", 'cot0shot.math teacher_answer': '696310226', 'cot0shot.math teacher_result': True, 'cot0shot.math teacher_thinking_CoT': "\nFirst, I need to add the two numbers 575,113,071 and 121,197,155.\n\nI'll start by aligning the numbers by their place values to ensure each digit is added correctly.\n\nAdding the digits in the ones place: 1 + 5 equals 6.\n\nNext, I'll add the digits in the tens place: 7 + 5 equals 12. I'll write down 2 and carry over 1 to the next place.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place: 0 + 1 plus the carried over 1 equals 2.\n\nIn the thousands place: 3 + 7 equals 10. I'll write down 0 and carry over 1.\n\nFor the ten thousands place: 1 + 9 plus the carried over 1 equals 11. I'll write down 1 and carry over 1.\n\nIn the hundred thousands place: 1 + 1 plus the carried over 1 equals 3.\n\nNext, in the millions place: 5 + 1 equals 6.\n\nFinally, in the hundred millions place: 5 + 1 equals 6.\n\nCombining all these results gives me the final sum.\n", 'cot0shot.math teacher_output_CoT': ".\n\n# Question:.\nWhat is the sum of 575,113,071 and 121,197,155?.\n\n# Reasoning:.\n\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.\n\n1. **Align the numbers by their place values:**.\n\n```.\n  575,113,071.\n+ 121,197,155.\n--------------.\n```.\n\n2. **Add the digits starting from the right (ones place):**.\n\n```.\n      1 (ones place).\n     7 + 5 = 12 → Write down 2, carry over 1.\n    0 + 1 + 1 (carry) = 2.\n    3 + 7 = 10 → Write down 0, carry over 1.\n    1 + 9 + 1 (carry) = 11 → Write down 1, carry over 1.\n    1 + 1 + 1 (carry) = 3.\n    5 + 1 = 6.\n    5 + 1 = 6.\n```.\n\n3. **Combine the results:**.\n\n```.\n  575,113,071.\n+ 121,197,155.\n--------------.\n  696,310,226.\n```.\n\n# Answer:", 'role': 'math teacher', 'biasanswer': '696510226'} 54%|#####4    | 272/500 [17:31<08:53,  2.34s/it]
