:**\n\n```\n  131,755,873\n+ 603,928,666\n--------------\n  735,684,539\n```\n\n# Answer:\n\nTherefore, the final computed sum is \\(\\boxed{735,\\!684,\\!539}\\).", 'cot0shot.math teacher_thinking': "\nFirst, I need to add the two numbers 131,755,873 and 603,928,666.\n\nI'll start by aligning the numbers by their place values to ensure each digit is added correctly.\n\nAdding the digits in the ones place: 3 + 6 equals 9.\n\nNext, I'll add the digits in the tens place: 7 + 6 equals 13. I'll write down 3 and carry over 1 to the next place.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place: 8 + 6 plus the carried-over 1 equals 15. I'll write down 5 and carry over 1.\n\nIn the thousands place: 5 + 8 plus the carried-over 1 equals 14. I'll write down 4 and carry over 1.\n\nFor the ten thousands place: 7 + 2 plus the carried-over 1 equals 10. I'll write down 0 and carry over 1.\n\nIn the hundred thousands place: 1 + 9 plus the carried-over 1 equals 11. I'll write down 1 and carry over 1.\n\nNext, in the millions place: 3 + 3 plus the carried-over 1 equals 7.\n\nFinally, in the ten millions place: 1 + 6 equals 7.\n\nCombining all the results, the sum of 131,755,873 and 603,928,666 is 735,684,539.\n", 'cot0shot.math teacher_answer': '735684539', 'cot0shot.math teacher_result': True, 'cot0shot.math teacher_thinking_CoT': ".\nFirst, I need to add the two numbers 131,755,873 and 603,928,666.\n\nI'll start by aligning the numbers by their place values to ensure each digit is added correctly.\n\nAdding the digits in the ones place: 3 + 6 equals 9.\n\nNext, I'll add the digits in the tens place: 7 + 6 equals 13. I'll write down 3 and carry over 1 to the next place.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place: 8 + 6 plus the carried-over 1 equals 15. I'll write down 5 and carry over 1.\n\nIn the thousands place: 5 + 8 plus the carried-over 1 equals 14. I'll write down 4 and carry over 1.\n\nFor the ten thousands place: 7 + 2 plus the carried-over 1 equals 10. I'll write down 0 and carry over 1.\n\nIn the hund