dreds place: 4 + 6 equals 10. I'll write down 0 and carry over 1 to the thousands place.\n\nIn the thousands place: 8 + 8 + 1 equals 17. I'll write down 7 and carry over 1 to the ten-thousands place.\n\nFor the ten-thousands place: 2 + 1 + 1 equals 4.\n\nIn the hundred-thousands place: 1 + 7 equals 8.\n\nNext, in the millions place: 5 + 5 equals 10. I'll write down 0 and carry over 1 to the ten-millions place.\n\nIn the ten-millions place: 2 + 8 + 1 equals 11. I'll write down 1 and carry over 1 to the hundred-millions place.\n\nFinally, in the hundred-millions place: 2 + 6 + 1 equals 9", 'cot0shot.math teacher_output_CoT': "\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of 252,128,435 and 685,718,605?\n\n# Reasoning:\n\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.\n\n```\n    252,128,435\n  + 685,718,605\n  ==============\n```\n\n1. **Ones place:**  \n   \\(5 + 5 = 10\\)  \n   Write down **0** and carry over **1**.\n\n2. **Tens place:**  \n   \\(3 + 0 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 4\\)  \n   Write down **4**.\n\n3. **Hundreds place:**  \n   \\(4 + 6 = 10\\)  \n   Write down **0** and carry over **1**.\n\n4. **Thousands place:**  \n   \\(8 + 8 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 17\\)  \n   Write down **7** and carry over **1**.\n\n5. **Ten-thousands place:**  \n   \\(2 + 1 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 4\\)  \n   Write down **4**.\n\n6. **Hundred-thousands place:**  \n   \\(1 + 7 = 8\\)  \n   Write down **8**.\n\n7. **Millions place:**  \n   \\(5 + 5 = 10\\)  \n   Write down **0** and carry over **1**.\n\n8. **Ten-millions place:**  \n   \\(2 + 8 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 11\\)  \n   Write down **1** and carry over **1**.\n\n9. **Hundred-millions place:**  \n   \\(2 + 6 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 9\\)  \n   Write down **9**.\n\nPutting it all together, the final sum is:\n\n# Answer:\n\\[\n\\boxed{937,\\!847,\\!040}\n\\]", 'role': 'math teacher', 'biasanswer': '934847040'}
