2849}\n\\]", 'cot0shot.math teacher_thinking': '\nFirst, I will align the two numbers vertically to ensure that each digit is in the correct place value.\n\nNext, I will add the digits starting from the rightmost digit (the ones place) and move to the left.\n\nIf the sum of any two digits is 10 or more, I will carry over the extra value to the next higher place value.\n\nI will continue this process for each digit, ensuring that all place values are correctly added and any necessary carrying is accounted for.\n\nFinally, after adding all the digits, I will arrive at the total sum of the two numbers.\n', 'cot0shot.math teacher_answer': '765222849', 'cot0shot.math teacher_result': True, 'cot0shot.math teacher_thinking_CoT': '\nFirst, I will align the two numbers vertically to ensure that each digit is in the correct place value.\n\nNext, I will add the digits starting from the rightmost digit (the ones place) and move to the left.\n\nIf the sum of any two digits is 10 or more, I will carry over the extra value to the next higher place value.\n\nI will continue this process for each digit, ensuring that all place values are correctly added and any necessary carrying is accounted for.\n\nFinally, after adding all the digits, I will arrive at the total sum of the two numbers.\n', 'cot0shot.math teacher_output_CoT': ".\n\n# Question:.\nWhat is the sum of 412690038 and 352532811?.\n\n# Reasoning:.\n\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit, starting from the rightmost digit (the ones place) and moving to the left.\n\n```.\n    412690038.\n  + 352532811.\n  ============.\n```.\n\n1. **Ones place:**  .\n   \\(8 + 1 = 9\\).\n\n2. **Tens place:**  .\n   \\(3 + 1 = 4\\).\n\n3. **Hundreds place:**  .\n   \\(0 + 8 = 8\\).\n\n4. **Thousands place:**  .\n   \\(0 + 2 = 2\\).\n\n5. **Ten-thousands place:**  .\n   \\(9 + 3 = 12\\)  .\n   Write down **2** and carry over **1** to the next place.\n\n6. **Hundred-thousands place:**  .\n   \\(6 + 5 + 1 (carry) = 12\\)  .\n   Write down **2** and carry over **1** to the next place.\n\n7. **Millions place:**  .\n   \\(2 + 2 + 1 (carry) = 5\\).\n\n8. **Ten-millions place:**  .\n   \\(1 + 5 = 6\\).\n\n9. **Hundred-millions place:**  .\n   \\(4 + 3 = 7\\).\n\nPutting it all together, the sum is:.\n\n\\[", 'role': 'math teacher', 'biasanswer': '765222840'} 77%|#######7  | 386/500 [24:31<04:17,  2.26s/it]
