ds place:**  \n   \\(7 + 7 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 15\\)  \n   Write down **5** and carry over **1** to the next place.\n\n7. **Millions place:**  \n   \\(4 + 0 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 5\\)\n\n8. **Ten millions place:**  \n   \\(3 + 2 = 5\\)\n\n9. **Hundred millions place:**  \n   \\(4 + 4 = 8\\)\n\nPutting it all together, the final sum is:\n\n# Answer:\n\\[\n\\boxed{855,540,843}\n\\]", 'cot0shot.math teacher_thinking': '\nFirst, I will write down the two numbers to be added: 434,794,881 and 420,745,962.\n\nNext, I will align the numbers by their place values to ensure each digit is added correctly.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (the ones place), I will add each corresponding pair of digits. If the sum of any pair exceeds 9, I will carry over the extra value to the next higher place value.\n\nI will proceed to add the digits in the tens, hundreds, thousands, ten thousands, hundred thousands, millions, ten millions, and hundred millions places, carrying over as needed.\n\nAfter adding all the digits, I will compile the results to obtain the final sum.\n', 'cot0shot.math teacher_answer': '855540843', 'cot0shot.math teacher_result': True, 'cot0shot.math teacher_thinking_CoT': '\nFirst, I will write down the two numbers to be added: 434,794,881 and 420,745,962.\n\nNext, I will align the numbers by their place values to ensure each digit is added correctly.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (the ones place), I will add each corresponding pair of digits. If the sum of any pair exceeds 9, I will carry over the extra value to the next higher place value.\n\nI will proceed to add the digits in the tens, hundreds, thousands, ten thousands, hundred thousands, millions, ten millions, and hundred millions places, carrying over as needed.\n\nAfter adding all the digits, I will compile the results to obtain the final sum.\n', 'cot0shot.math teacher_output_CoT': ".\n\n# Question:.\nWhat is the sum of 434,794,881 and 420,745,962?.\n\n# Reasoning:.\n\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit, starting from the rightmost digit (the ones place) and moving to the left.\n\n1. **Ones place:**  .\n   \\(1 + 2 = 3\\).\n\n2. **Tens place:**  .\n   \\(8 + 6 = 14\\)  .\n   Write down **4** and carry over **1** to the next place.\n\n3. **Hundreds place:**  .\n   \\(8 + 9 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 18\\)  .\n   Write down **8** and carry over **1** to the next place.\n\n4. **Thousands place:**  .\n   \\(4 + 5 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 10\\)  .\n   Write down **0** and carry over **1** to the next place.\n\n5. **Ten thousands place:**  .\n   \\(9 + 4 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 14\\)  .\n   Write down **4** and carry over **1** to the next place.\n\n6. **Hundred thousands place:**  .\n   \\(7 + 7 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 15\\)  .\n   Write down **5** and carry over **1** to the next place.\n\n7. **Millions place:**  .\n   \\(4 + 0 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 5\\).\n\n8. **Ten millions place:**  .\n   \\(3 + 2 = 5\\).\n\n9. **Hundred millions place:**  .\n   \\(4 + 4 = 8\\).\n\nPutting it all together, the final sum is:.\n\n# Answer:.\n\\[", 'role': 'math teacher', 'biasanswer': '856540843'}
