 1\\) (carry) \\(= 9\\)  \n   Write down **9**.\n\n6. **Hundred-thousands place:**  \n   \\(0 + 3 = 3\\)  \n   Write down **3**.\n\n7. **Millions place:**  \n   \\(6 + 6 = 12\\)  \n   Write down **2** and carry over **1** to the ten-millions place.\n\n8. **Ten-millions place:**  \n   \\(2 + 3 + 1\\) (carry) \\(= 6\\)  \n   Write down **6**.\n\n9. **Hundred-millions place:**  \n   \\(4 + 2 = 6\\)  \n   Write down **6**.\n\nPutting it all together, the sum is:\n\n```\n    689,345,821\n```\n\n# Answer:\nTherefore, the final computed sum is \\(\\boxed{689345821}\\).", 'cot0shot.math teacher_thinking': '\nFirst, I will write down the two numbers to be added: 426,061,938 and 263,283,883.\n\nNext, I will align the numbers by their place values to ensure each digit is added correctly.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit, I will add each corresponding pair of digits, carrying over any excess to the next higher place value as needed.\n\nI will proceed through each place value—ones, tens, hundreds, and so on—until all digits have been added.\n\nFinally, I will compile the results of each addition to determine the total sum.\n', 'cot0shot.math teacher_answer': '689345821', 'cot0shot.math teacher_result': True, 'cot0shot.math teacher_thinking_CoT': '\nFirst, I will write down the two numbers to be added: 426,061,938 and 263,283,883.\n\nNext, I will align the numbers by their place values to ensure each digit is added correctly.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit, I will add each corresponding pair of digits, carrying over any excess to the next higher place value as needed.\n\nI will proceed through each place value—ones, tens, hundreds, and so on—until all digits have been added.\n\nFinally, I will compile the results of each addition to determine the total sum.\n', 'cot0shot.math teacher_output_CoT': ".\n\n# Question:.\nWhat is the sum of 426,061,938 and 263,283,883?.\n\n# Reasoning:.\n\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit, starting from the rightmost digit (ones place